        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Hardware Hacking: Discovering a DoS in NetGear Router]]></title>
        <id>https://risk3sixty.com/blog/hardware-hacking-discovering-a-dos-in-netgear-router</id>
        <link href="https://risk3sixty.com/blog/hardware-hacking-discovering-a-dos-in-netgear-router"/>
        <updated>2025-12-09T20:45:33.215Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<a class="elementor-post__thumbnail__link" href="https://risk3sixty.com/blog/hardware-hacking-discovering-a-dos-in-netgear-router" tabindex="-1">
			<div class="elementor-post__thumbnail"><img loading="lazy" width="300" height="200" src="https://risk3sixty.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/netgear-vuln-300x200.png" class="attachment-medium size-medium wp-image-32017" alt=""></div>
		</a>
				<div class="elementor-post__text">
				<h3 class="elementor-post__title">
			<a href="https://risk3sixty.com/blog/hardware-hacking-discovering-a-dos-in-netgear-router">
				Hardware Hacking: Discovering a DoS in NetGear Router			</a>
		</h3>
				<div class="elementor-post__excerpt">
			<p>Our security team identified an unauthenticated Denial-of-Service (DoS) vulnerability affecting a Netgear router’s web management interface. During routine testing of an internet-connected device, we found that a flaw in the /goform/Unauth endpoint allows any network user to crash and reboot the router, disrupting downstream services. Despite early disclosure and multiple follow-ups, no guidance has been issued by Netgear as of their latest security updates. This post details the discovery process, failed firmware update attempts, hardware-level investigation, and the conditions under which the vulnerability can be triggered.</p>
		</div>
					<div class="elementor-post__read-more-wrapper">
		
		<a class="elementor-post__read-more" href="https://risk3sixty.com/blog/hardware-hacking-discovering-a-dos-in-netgear-router" aria-label="Read more about Hardware Hacking: Discovering a DoS in NetGear Router" tabindex="-1">
			Read More		</a>

					</div>
				</div>]]></content>
